    "disposition": "bounded-presentation-and-origin-preservation",
    "inference": "These outcomes support control candidates for specific allegations about nameplate clipping, missing icon delivery, escaped source rendering and the tested origin access restrictions. They do not establish that either whole patch is defect-free.",
    "limits": [
      "Two adjacent changes in one presentation sequence, not independent incidents.",
      "Named viewport/browser/security checks do not prove universal accessibility, security or aesthetic approval.",
      "No native reviewer, corpus admission or ranking.",
      "No browser tab favicon UI, universal accessibility, other browser engines or untested viewport/security behavior is assessed."
    ],
    "observations": [
      "Six original builder and HTTP-server executions completed: three revisions, two repetitions, with synthetic publication input and pinned Chromium 153.0.8010.12.",
      "At 320, 768 and 1280 CSS-pixel widths the nameplate and document remain within the viewport. The nameplate accessibility snapshot identifies a link named AI Newsroom at / in all recorded views.",
      "Direct inspection of the four retained screenshots shows the original text nameplate, the new green AI mark beside Newsroom at mobile width, the desktop mark, and a rendered green square AI icon.",
      "The icon revision serves the original SVG bytes with image/svg+xml and references /icon.svg; both prior revisions return 404 for that asset.",
      "Each revision serves pages, CSS and RSS, refuses tested private/dot/traversal/symlink paths with 404 and POST with 501, retains original origin headers, and leaves the publication database unchanged during reads.",
      "Synthetic HTML-like title and pick text render literally with no DOM scripts. The original source story remains in SQLite and its title survives RSS generation.",
      "Only the icon revision ignores .playwright-mcp/probe.txt; the source-file control remains unignored."
    ],
